Kernel 2 — Identity, Invites, Role Authority, and Workshop Asset Floor
Purpose

Establish the first durable foundation for user identity, access control, producer/director authority, invite-driven role assignment, and workshop-based asset ingestion.

This kernel is not about visual polish.
It is about making the system trustworthy enough to build on.

Scope

Build the minimum viable system for:

producer signup
account login/re-entry
password storage and session auth
invite-based access and role assignment
production-scoped director authority
workshop asset upload and auto-clamping
asset ownership metadata
map visibility driven by role + grants
Identity Rules
Signup
requires email
requires handle
requires password
requires display name
Login
uses handle + password
Recovery
producer and users must have a path to regain access later
preferred first implementation: email reset link
Password Handling
passwords must be hashed securely
no raw password storage
no role self-assignment through client payload
Role Authority Rules
Producer
owns the Location
controls venues, storage, and appointments
may appoint one or more Directors
may restrict Director access to venues
Director
authority is scoped to assigned Production
may invite Cast/Crew to that Production
may invite Audience to associated venues/sessions if allowed
Cast / Crew
may join assigned Productions
may invite Audience if policy permits
Audience
may be admitted by invite/ticket/will-call flow
does not gain direct production authority
Invite Rules

Invites are a general access mechanism, not a privileged admin-only feature.

Each invite should carry:

inviter identity
target role
optional production scope
optional venue scope
expiration
single-use or limited-use behavior

Examples:

producer → director
director → cast
director → crew
cast/crew → audience
audience self-arrival via public venue access where allowed

Will-call behavior:

audience invite should automatically assign audience role on acceptance
Map / Access Rules

The landing map is a permission surface.

Visibility should be determined by:

role
assigned venue access
explicit grants

Examples:

public users see only limited map areas
signed-in users see more
audience+ may see museum/info-booth/public-facing areas
cast/crew may see library, production houses, school, etc. as granted
directors may see most venues by courtesy unless limited by producer
production-specific grants allow entry to production venue(s)

Fog of war is acceptable and encouraged.

Workshop Rules

The workshop is a special venue/environment for making things.

Its first job is not beauty.
Its first job is controlled asset ingestion.

First supported workshop action
upload image asset
On upload, system must:
validate file type
validate size
validate actual file signature if practical
auto-clamp/resize
assign ownership metadata
store result on producer-owned server storage
make asset available for later production use
Initial allowed asset types
png
jpg
jpeg
webp
Initial limits
max file size: 10 MB
max source dimensions: 4096 x 4096
generate standard sizes:
512
1024
2048
Initial exclusions
no svg
no animated gifs
no video yet
no audio yet
no arbitrary documents
Asset Ownership Rules

Assets do not automatically become producer property just because they are used.

Initial ownership states:

personal
uploader-owned
lent for use
production_licensed
usable for a given production
library_owned
copied/promoted to producer library with explicit permission

System must record:

uploader
owner state
storage path
source file metadata
derived sizes
Storage Rules
assets stored on producer’s own server instance
file storage should be organized in per-producer paths
metadata stored in DB
served in controlled way, not blindly trusted
Non-Goals

Do not build in this kernel:

stage rendering
browser theater UI
note-card flow
speech overlay visuals
black box venue tools
marketplace
LMS records
multi-server competition logic
advanced audience segmentation
video/audio upload pipeline
Success Criteria

Kernel 2 passes when:

a producer can sign up with email/handle/password
that producer can log out and log back in with handle/password
password storage is secure and not raw
producer can create or issue an invite for a director
director invite acceptance results in correct role assignment
role is system-assigned, not client-asserted
workshop accepts an image upload
upload is auto-clamped into standard sizes
asset ownership metadata is stored correctly
uploaded asset is associated to producer storage and available for later production use
map visibility changes correctly based on role + grants
Required Report-Back Focus

Builder must explicitly report:

auth/session method used
password hashing method
invite token behavior
storage paths used
clamp/resize pipeline used
file safety limits enforced
operator steps for local dev vs install truth
blockers and operator actions